  "term": "spike-and-wave discharges",
  "definition": "Spike-and-wave discharges are epileptiform EEG activity patterns generated within the cortico-thalamo-cortical circuit. In this source, they are described as arising from a focal network that can spread to surrounding areas and are linked with transitions between normal brain activity and absence-seizure activity.",
